Ladybird’s runtime.openOptionsPage() reuses a tab already showing
the options page, or opens one, as Chromium’s ExtensionTabUtil::
OpenOptionsPage() does through its singleton-tab navigation; Gecko shows
an options_ui page inside about:addons, which Ladybird doesn’t have.
An extension without an options page gets Chromium’s “Could not create
an options page.”, and runtime.setUninstallURL() takes only an http or
https URL, failing otherwise with Chromium’s “Invalid URL” text.
